# SurrealDB JavaScript / TypeScript SDK

- Use the official `surrealdb` package (the old `surrealdb.js` name is deprecated).
- Connect to the RPC endpoint, then select namespace/database, then sign in:
  ```ts
  import { Surreal } from "surrealdb";

  const db = new Surreal();
  await db.connect("http://127.0.0.1:8000/rpc");
  await db.use({ namespace: "real_agent", database: "v1" });
  await db.signin({ username: "root", password: "root" });

  const result = await db.query("SELECT * FROM agent WHERE tenant = $t", { t: "acme" });
  await db.close();
  ```
- Always pass variables as the second `query` argument; never string-concatenate
  untrusted values into SurrealQL.
- `db.query` returns an array, one entry per statement — index into it.
- Use `db.live(table, cb)` / `LIVE SELECT` for real-time subscriptions instead of polling.
- Close the connection (`db.close()`) when done; reuse one `Surreal` instance per app.
